  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 2.3. Increased capacity of Member States to engage in a forward-looking international labour standards policy</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Ministry of Economic Development (MED) submitted reports due in 2022 (C029, C105, C138, C182, C185) before 1 September 2022 and provided replies to the comments of the ILO supervisory bodies. MED submitted reports due in 2023 on C100 and C111 responding to the comments of the ILO supervisory bodies before 1 September. ILO provided technical assistance and consultations to the MED to help to prepare reports for the supervisory bodies in 2022 and 2023.

ILO has provided a dedicated training for 4 government officials from Ministry of Economic Development and Ministry of Transport to fulfill the reporting and complying with reporting obligations on the application, in law and in practice, of the MLC, 2006.Four government officials from MED and Ministry of Transport (MoT) attended ITC training in 2022 &#x201d;Reporting on the MLC, 2006&#x201d;.</narrative>
   </description>
